solutionMd:
## The idea

Every call to knows(a, b) rules somebody out: if a knows b, then a is not the celebrity (the celebrity knows nobody); if a does not know b, then b is not the celebrity (everybody knows the celebrity). So one pass keeps a single **candidate**: whenever the candidate knows someone, that person becomes the new candidate. After n − 1 calls one candidate is left — but it still has to be **checked**, because there may be no celebrity at all.

## Step by step

1. candidate = 0.
2. For i = 1 … n−1: if knows(candidate, i), candidate = i.
3. Check: for every other person i, the candidate must NOT know i, and i MUST know the candidate. If either fails → −1.
4. Otherwise return the candidate.

## Worked example

**Input:** 4 people; person 2 is the celebrity

| Step | What happens |
|---|---|
| candidate 0 | knows(0, 1)? say no → 1 cannot be the celebrity, keep 0 |
| i = 2 | knows(0, 2)? yes → 0 is not the celebrity → candidate = 2 |
| i = 3 | knows(2, 3)? no → keep 2 |
| check | 2 knows nobody, and 0, 1, 3 all know 2 → confirmed |

**Result:** 2

## Cost

At most 3(n − 1) calls to knows: n − 1 in the first pass and at most 2(n − 1) in the check. O(1) memory.

## The code (C#, compiled and tested against every part of the question)

```csharp
public static class Celebrity {

    // knows(a, b) is an expensive call — use as few as possible.
    public static int Find(int n, Func<int, int, bool> knows) {
        if (n <= 0) return -1;

        // Pass 1: whoever the candidate knows replaces it.
        int candidate = 0;
        for (int i = 1; i < n; i++) {
            if (knows(candidate, i)) candidate = i;
        }

        // Pass 2: the survivor must really be a celebrity.
        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            if (i == candidate) continue;               // never ask knows(x, x)
            if (knows(candidate, i)) return -1;         // a celebrity knows nobody
            if (!knows(i, candidate)) return -1;        // and everybody knows the celebrity
        }
        return candidate;
    }
}
```

